  "notes": [
    "Wowhead (classic and forever) beast listviews could not be read: WebFetch strips the embedded Listview script data, direct curl got HTTP 403, and later WebFetch calls to wowhead also returned 403. So there are no wowhead beast observations. Wowhead does have a Forever section: the classic spell=17255 page links to /forever/spell=17255/bite (Bite, 35 Focus, 10 s cooldown, damage effect value 17). The classic spell=17253 page showed Bite, 35 Focus, damage effect value 7; rank/level/TP were not visible in the fetched text, so the wowhead-classic rank 1 spellId rests on the page URL/title only.",
    "warcraft.wiki.gg: the Bite article has one Classic stat block (Level 1, 35 Focus, 7 to 9 damage, '8 ranks') and no per-rank table or teaching-beast list. The Pet abilities (Classic) table gives Bite level 1, 1 TP (recorded as rank 1); the Bite article's external links include wowhead classic spell=17253. No rank 2-4 data and no beast list. Bite_(hunter_pet_ability) and Bite_(Classic) return 404; Training_point has no Bite table.",
    "classicdb.ch (vanilla DB) spell pages: R1 17253 level 1 '7 to 10 damage'; R2 17255 level 8 '16 to 19'; R3 17256 level 16 '24 to 29'; R4 17257 level 24 '31 to 38'. No TP, icon, or taught-by list could be read. Petopia damage: R1 7-9, R2 16-18, R3 24-28, R4 31-37 (small top-end differences from classicdb; damage is not in the schema). classicdb NPC pages showed no level/abilities, so they were not used for beasts.",
    "petopia-classic: one abilities page (abilities.php#bite) lists the Bite 1-4 beasts with family, level, zone and wowhead NPC links (classic.wowhead.com/npc=<id>). All npcIds in this file come from those links. Petopia shows no rare/elite markers. It labels dungeon zones with '(Dungeon)' (Wailing Caverns: Deviate Crocolisk, Kresh; Blackfathom Deeps: Aku'mai Fisher, Ghamoo-ra, Aku'mai Snapjaw), and that suffix was stripped from the zone names here. Petopia's Bite icon image is ability_druid_ferociousbite.png (a site image, not necessarily the game icon). icon is left null because no game-data source showed it.",
    "warcrafttavern (warcrafttavern.com/wow-classic/hunter-pets/<skin>/ pages, 'Skills When Tamed' field): all wolf, spider, crocolisk and turtle skin pages were checked. It matched petopia for 56 of 57 beasts (same names, ranks, levels, zones) and gives no NPC IDs, so its entries were attached by name. Cranky Benj (petopia: rank 4, level 32, Alterac Mountains) was not found on any warcrafttavern turtle page. Wildthorn Stalker (20-21, Ashenvale) shows 'Skills When Tamed: None' on warcrafttavern and is not on petopia's list. warcrafttavern and petopia agree exactly, so they may share an upstream data origin; treat their agreement with some caution.",
    "Elite/rare flags: neither source marked any beast, so the flags are omitted. Several entries are named mobs (e.g. Githyiss the Vile, Timber, Lady Sathrah, Shanda the Spinner, Besseleth, Chatter, Lupos, Creepthess, Naraxis, Cranky Benj, Night Web Matriarch) or dungeon bosses (Kresh, Ghamoo-ra) that may be rare or elite, but no source confirmed it.",
    "Forever-specific: the GitHub wiki classic-hunter/forever-hunter 'Pet Families and Abilities' (https://github-wiki-see.page/m/classic-hunter/forever-hunter/wiki/Pet-Families-and-Abilities) says 'Forever guarantees that every family can learn either Bite or Claw, although not every family can learn both' and lists the Bite families as Bat, Bear, Boar, Carrion Bird, Cat, Crocolisk, Gorilla, Hyena, Raptor, Spider, Tallstrider, Turtle, Wind Serpent, Wolf (the same as the warcraft.wiki.gg Classic list). No Forever-specific rank or beast data was found. Per both beast sources, only wolf, spider, crocolisk and turtle beasts teach ranks 1-4."
